{"chunk_id": "beca24edc98d", "text": "As the battle rages, the sound of Drona\u2019s advancing chariot terrifies the Pandava-allied Prabhadrakas while multiple duels erupt across the field. Chitrasena blocks Chekitana to protect Bhishma, and Dussasana struggles to restrain Arjuna, who nevertheless drives back the Kaurava forces. In the midst of the chaos, Drona penetrates the Pandava ranks and speaks to his son after observing a series of dire omens\u2014strange celestial signs, frightened animals, trembling idols, and the sun losing its radiance. Interpreting these portents, he predicts that Arjuna will press forward to slay Bhishma, especially by placing Sikhandin before him, since Bhishma refuses to strike Sikhandin. Though foreseeing terrible slaughter, Drona still commands his son to fight, invoking Kshatriya duty and warning that Arjuna\u2019s advance will bring catastrophic carnage to the Kaurava host.\nDrona foresees ominous signs of Bhishma\u2019s impending fall and instructs his son to confront Arjuna and Sikhandin as the Pandava assault intensifies.\nThemes: ominous portents, duty of a warrior, approaching fall of Bhishma, father-son counsel, battle strategy", "vector": [-0.008888735435903072, -0.01614276133477688, -0.01818614825606346, 0.024384424090385437, 0.009733336046338081, 0.0277764480561018, -0.023648804053664207, -0.0032762312330305576, -0.02893436700105667, -0.011245442554354668, 0.012669002637267113, 0.02103326842188835, -0.0046793571673333645, 0.00814630463719368, 0.008711641654372215, 0.007594590075314045, 0.043374303728342056, -0.0037121539935469627, 0.02510642074048519, -0.024289065971970558, -0.015883931890130043, -0.005796409212052822, 0.014358202926814556, 0.009624355472624302, -0.02559683471918106, 0.031713373959064484, 0.0023277588188648224, -0.030950509011745453, -0.006838536821305752, -0.006719339173287153, -0.006320878863334656, 0.0019037560559809208, 0.00041655305540189147, 0.0034465135540813208, -0.018267884850502014, 0.0044579901